Q: Geoserver proxy behind nginx - can only login to web interface from one out of three domains A: <p>geoserver-2.28.2</p>
<h1>Basic Setting</h1>
<p>3 site name:</p>
<ul>
<li>demo1.example.local</li>
<li>demo2.example.local</li>
<li>demo3.example.local</li>
</ul>
<p>Host (Your machine)</p>
<h2>/etc/hosts</h2>
<p>ADD ip and name, ip is your host address. (here is 10.42.0.123 , replace the ip for your own)</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>10.42.0.123  demo1.example.local
10.42.0.123  demo2.example.local
10.42.0.123  demo3.example.local
</code></pre>
<h1>geoserver</h1>
<h2>Download zip</h2>
<p>geoserver-2.28.2-bin.zip</p>
<h2>unzip</h2>
<p>get directory: geoserver-2.28.2-bin</p>
<h2>Change config</h2>
<h3>geoserver-2.28.2-bin/etc/jetty.xml</h3>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;New id=&quot;httpConfig&quot; class=&quot;org.eclipse.jetty.server.HttpConfiguration&quot;&gt;
...
&lt;!-- Uncomment to enable handling of X-Forwarded- style headers --&gt;
        &lt;Call name=&quot;addCustomizer&quot;&gt;
            &lt;Arg&gt;&lt;New class=&quot;org.eclipse.jetty.server.ForwardedRequestCustomizer&quot;/&gt;&lt;/Arg&gt;
        &lt;/Call&gt;

&lt;/New&gt;
</code></pre>
<h3>geoserver-2.28.2-bin/webapps/geoserver/WEB-INF/web.xml</h3>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>    &lt;display-name&gt;GeoServer&lt;/display-name&gt;
    &lt;!--- ADD THIS --&gt;
    &lt;context-param&gt;
        &lt;param-name&gt;GEOSERVER_CSRF_WHITELIST&lt;/param-name&gt;
        &lt;param-value&gt;demo1.example.local,demo2.example.local,demo3.example.local&lt;/param-value&gt;
    &lt;/context-param&gt;
    ...
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li><p>Use JDK 17</p>
</li>
<li><p>Start geoserver</p>
</li>
</ul>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>export GEOSERVER_HOME=/home/demo/geoserver-2.28.2-bin
cd $GEOSERVER_HOME/bin
./startup.sh
</code></pre>
<h1>NGINX Proxy</h1>
<p>create a directory: <code>docker-nginx-geoserver</code></p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>docker-nginx-geoserver
├── docker-compose.yml
├── etc
│   └── nginx
│       ├── sites-available
│       │   ├── geoserver.conf
│       │   └── proxy_params
│       └── ssl
│           ├── demo1.example.local.crt
│           ├── demo1.example.local.key
│           ├── demo2.example.local.crt
│           ├── demo2.example.local.key
│           ├── demo3.example.local.crt
│           └── demo3.example.local.key
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>create SSL cert at docker-nginx-geoserver/etc/ssl</li>
<li>create a directory: docker-nginx-geoserver/etc/nginx/sites-available</li>
</ul>
<h2>geoserver.conf</h2>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>server {
    listen 80;
    server_name demo1.example.local demo2.example.local demo3.example.local;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name demo1.example.local;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/demo1.example.local.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/demo1.example.local.key;

    location / {
    proxy_cookie_path / &quot;/; HTTPOnly; Secure; SameSite=None&quot;;
        proxy_pass http://host.docker.internal:8080;
        include /etc/nginx/conf.d/proxy_params;
    }
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name demo2.example.local;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/demo2.example.local.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/demo2.example.local.key;

    location / {
    proxy_cookie_path / &quot;/; HTTPOnly; Secure; SameSite=None&quot;;
        proxy_pass http://host.docker.internal:8080;
        include /etc/nginx/conf.d/proxy_params;
    }
}


server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name demo3.example.local;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/demo3.example.local.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/demo3.example.local.key;

    location / {
    proxy_cookie_path / &quot;/; HTTPOnly; Secure; SameSite=None&quot;;
        proxy_pass http://host.docker.internal:8080;
        include /etc/nginx/conf.d/proxy_params;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<h2>proxy_params</h2>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>proxy_set_header Host $host;

proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 443;

client_max_body_size 100M;

proxy_buffers 16 64k;
proxy_buffer_size 128k;
proxy_connect_timeout 600;
proxy_send_timeout 600;
proxy_read_timeout 600;
proxy_redirect http://$host/ https://$host/;
</code></pre>
<h2>docker-compose.yml</h2>
<pre class="lang-yaml prettyprint-override"><code>version: '3.8'

services:
  nginx-proxy:
    image: nginx:latest
    container_name: nginx-geoserver
    restart: always
    ports:
      - &quot;80:80&quot;
      - &quot;443:443&quot;
    volumes:
      - ./etc/nginx/sites-available:/etc/nginx/conf.d:ro
      - ./etc/nginx/ssl:/etc/nginx/ssl:ro

    extra_hosts:
      - &quot;host.docker.internal:host-gateway&quot;
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Start NGINX</li>
</ul>
<p>at directory: docker-nginx-geoserver</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>docker-compose up -d
</code></pre>
<h1>Test</h1>
<h2>Test-1</h2>
<p><a href="https://demo1.example.local/geoserver" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://demo1.example.local/geoserver</a></p>
<p>(if you get 502, this indicates that the geoserver has not yet started.)</p>
<p>user name: <code>admin</code>
password:  <code>geoserver</code></p>
